{{ tref('table07_ablation') }} and {{ fref('fig09_ablation') }} report one-factor changes to MAPLE-Net, each pretrained
with seed 0 and compared with MAPLE-Net seed 0 on all synthetic tasks and on real data at $n_{\mathrm{train}}$ = 512.
These comparisons must be read against the variation between pretraining seeds. Across its three seeds, MAPLE-Net's
mean ID NRMSE ranged over {{ num(SY.seed_spread['MAPLE-Net'].id_range, 4) }} and its mean OOD NRMSE over
{{ num(SY.seed_spread['MAPLE-Net'].ood_range, 4) }}.{% if SY.seed_spread['MAPLE-Net'].id[0] == SY.seed_spread['MAPLE-Net'].id | max %}
Seed 0 happened to be the least accurate of the three on the ID suite ({{ num(SY.seed_spread['MAPLE-Net'].id[0], 4) }}),
